# Construction A, the bridge from binary codes to lattices, and the extended Hamming code that builds the densest eight-
# dimensional packing. Given a binary code, the Construction A lattice is every integer vector whose reduction modulo two
# lies in the code, so the code's minimum distance becomes the lattice's minimum squared length and the code's weights
# become the lattice's shells. The eight-dimensional lattice comes from the extended Hamming code [8,4,4], whose sixteen
# codewords have a symmetric weight enumerator: one word of weight zero, fourteen of weight four, one of weight eight. The
# code contains the all-ones word, so complementation sends weight w to eight minus w, pairing weight zero with weight
# eight and fixing the central weight four. This file MODELS the weight classes and DEFINES complementation, then PROVES
# it is an involution pairing zero with eight and fixing four. The codeword count, the weight enumerator sum, and the
# perfect-packing identity of the parent Hamming code are recorded as machine-integer facts. The involution is proved over
# the actual weight-class type by induction.

# The weight classes of the extended Hamming codewords: weights zero, four and eight.
form weight-class
  case weight-zero
  case weight-four
  case weight-eight

# Complementing a codeword flips all eight bits, sending weight w to eight minus w: zero and eight swap, and the central
# weight four is fixed.
task complement
  take w, like weight-class
  like weight-class
  fork case, read w
    case weight-zero
      send back
        make weight-eight
    case weight-eight
      send back
        make weight-zero
    case weight-four
      send back
        make weight-four

# COMPLEMENTATION IS AN INVOLUTION: complementing a weight class twice returns it, complement (complement w) = w, for every
# class, so the weight enumerator is symmetric. Proved by induction over the three weight classes.
rule complementation-is-an-involution
  seat w, like weight-class
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call complement
        call complement
          read w
      read w
  fold w

# THE CENTRAL WEIGHT IS SELF-COMPLEMENTARY: weight four is fixed by complementation, complement weight-four = weight-four,
# the center of the symmetric enumerator.
rule the-central-weight-is-self-complementary
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call complement
        make weight-four
      make weight-four
  calm hold

# THE WEIGHT ENUMERATOR SUMS to the sixteen codewords as a machine-integer fact: 1 + 14 + 1 = 16, which is two to the
# fourth, the dimension-four code.
hold weight-enumerator-sums-to-sixteen
  call is-equal
    code 16
    call add
      code 1
      call add
        code 14
        code 1

# THE PARENT HAMMING CODE IS PERFECT: the [7,4,3] Hamming code's sixteen codewords each own a radius-one ball of eight
# points, and 16 * 8 = 128 = two to the seventh tiles the whole seven-bit space with no overlap or gap.
hold hamming-code-perfectly-tiles-the-space
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 16
      code 8
    code 128
